Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:59:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] fix(backend): read "localhost" in a database URL as
 127.0.0.1

Measured on the product owner's Windows machine with a Docker database:
connecting through the name localhost took 15,027 ms, through 127.0.0.1
19 ms, and a query took 0.4 ms either way. The 145 tests open many
connections, so they needed 393 s instead of a few seconds.

parse_database_url now maps the host name localhost to 127.0.0.1. Every
other host, including the IPv6 address [::1], is kept as written (D-102).

- core/env.py and core/tests/test_env.py (9 new tests, 1 updated).
- README, AGENTS.md and the Arabic guide: write 127.0.0.1, and run pytest
  from inside Qeeva-Backend/ (from the repository root it cannot find
  pyproject.toml and fails with "settings are not configured").
- Decision log: D-102. Plans updated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
